      {
        "width": 312,
        "height": 428,
        "id": "textfields-1735326172437",
        "type": "textfields",
        "data": {
          "fields": {
            "f1": "Shorten the following text without adding any new words: {text}",
            "f2": "Delete words in the following paragraph, while keeping grammaticality and readability. Only remove words, do not add any new words. Only return the revised paragraph, nothing else.\n\nParagraph:\n{text}",
            "f3": "Remove words in the following paragraph and return the revised paragraph. Only remove words. The paragraph should still be readable. \n\n{text}"
          },
          "vars": [
            "text"
          ],
          "refresh": false
        },
        "position": {
          "x": 48,
          "y": 112
        },
        "selected": false,
        "positionAbsolute": {
          "x": 48,
          "y": 112
        },
        "dragging": false
      },
      {
        "width": 312,
        "height": 525,
        "id": "textFieldsNode-1735326334600",
        "type": "textfields",
        "data": {
          "fields": {
            "f1": "The Peloponnesian War, a protracted and brutal conflict between Athens and Sparta, spanned several decades from 431 to 404 BC. It was a power struggle that showcased the clash between the democratic governance of Athens and the oligarchic system of Sparta, fundamentally altering the balance of power in the ancient Greek world. Thousands of soldiers and civilians lost their lives in drawn-out sieges and battles, such as the infamous Sicilian Expedition that decimated the Athenian fleet and army. This war saw the rise of alliances such as the Delian League, headed by Athens, and the Peloponnesian League, led by Sparta. Ultimately, the Spartan victory, achieved with Persian support, paved the way for a shifting political landscape that eventually saw the rise of Macedon and the decline of city-state dominance.",
            "f2": "The Punic Wars were a series of three conflicts fought between the Roman Republic and Carthage, characterized by their expansive scale and significant impact on the Mediterranean region, taking place between 264 and 146 BC. Initially, tensions escalated over control of Sicily and the Western Mediterranean, igniting the first of three major wars remembered most for Hannibal's audacious crossing of the Alps with his elephants during the Second Punic War. These wars witnessed colossal naval engagements and land battles, punctuated by the epic sieges of cities like Saguntum and Zama. The ultimate Roman victories led to the complete destruction of Carthage in the Third Punic War, ensuring Roman dominance over the Mediterranean for centuries to come. As a result, these wars facilitated Rome's transformation from a republic into a burgeoning empire, setting the stage for centuries of Roman cultural and political influence.",
            "f3": "The Greco-Persian Wars were a series of pivotal conflicts between the Achaemenid Empire and the city-states of Greece that occurred during much of the fifth century BC, forever changing the course of Western history. Initiated by the Persian expansion into territories held by Greek cities, these wars included legendary battles such as Marathon, Thermopylae, and Salamis, showcasing the valor and ingenuity of the vastly outnumbered Greek forces. The perseverance of Greek city-states against the might of a multinational empire was a testament to their determination to preserve their way of life, ultimately enabling the preservation of Greek culture and philosophy. The surprising Greek victories inspired a surge in confidence, leading to the Golden Age of Athens—a period marked by remarkable cultural and architectural advancements. These wars not only halted Persian expansion westward but also set the stage for the rise of Athens as a cultural and political powerhouse in the region."
          }
        },
        "position": {
          "x": -320,
          "y": 80
        },
        "selected": false,
        "positionAbsolute": {
          "x": -320,
          "y": 80
        },
        "dragging": false
      },
      {
        "width": 393,
        "height": 225,
        "id": "evalNode-1735326661375",
        "type": "evaluator",
        "data": {
          "language": "javascript",
          "code": "function evaluate(r) {\n  // Extract the words in the output\n  // and in the original paragraph\n  let outputWords = new Set(r.text.replace(/[.,\\/#!$%\\^&\\*;:{}=\\-_`~()]/g,\"\").toLowerCase().split(/\\s+/));\n  let origTextWords = new Set(r.var[\"text\"].replace(/[.,\\/#!$%\\^&\\*;:{}=\\-_`~()]/g,\"\").toLowerCase().split(/\\s+/));\n  let count = 0;\n  \n  // Count number of words the LLM added\n  outputWords.forEach(word => {\n    if (!origTextWords.has(word)) {\n      count++;\n    }\n  });\n\n  return count;\n}",
          "refresh": false,
          "title": "Count added words (errors)",
          "fields": [
            {
