    "prompt-1735326172437_0.json": {
      "Delete words in the following paragraph, while keeping grammaticality and readability. Only remove words, do not add any new words. Only return the revised paragraph, nothing else.\n\nParagraph:\nThe Punic Wars were a series of three conflicts fought between the Roman Republic and Carthage, characterized by their expansive scale and significant impact on the Mediterranean region, taking place between 264 and 146 BC. Initially, tensions escalated over control of Sicily and the Western Mediterranean, igniting the first of three major wars remembered most for Hannibal's audacious crossing of the Alps with his elephants during the Second Punic War. These wars witnessed colossal naval engagements and land battles, punctuated by the epic sieges of cities like Saguntum and Zama. The ultimate Roman victories led to the complete destruction of Carthage in the Third Punic War, ensuring Roman dominance over the Mediterranean for centuries to come. As a result, these wars facilitated Rome's transformation from a republic into a burgeoning empire, setting the stage for centuries of Roman cultural and political influence.": [
        {
          "prompt": 17,
          "uid": "bb3570d2-563c-4670-a2c7-52cd9a52086e",
          "responses": [
            56,
            57,
            58
          ],
          "llm": "Claude Haiku 4.5",
          "vars": {
            "prompt": 21,
            "text": 5
          },
          "metavars": {
            "__pt": "{prompt}",
            "LLM_0": "Claude Haiku 4.5"
          }
        }
      ],
      "Delete words in the following paragraph, while keeping grammaticality and readability. Only remove words, do not add any new words. Only return the revised paragraph, nothing else.\n\nParagraph:\nThe Peloponnesian War, a protracted and brutal conflict between Athens and Sparta, spanned several decades from 431 to 404 BC. It was a power struggle that showcased the clash between the democratic governance of Athens and the oligarchic system of Sparta, fundamentally altering the balance of power in the ancient Greek world. Thousands of soldiers and civilians lost their lives in drawn-out sieges and battles, such as the infamous Sicilian Expedition that decimated the Athenian fleet and army. This war saw the rise of alliances such as the Delian League, headed by Athens, and the Peloponnesian League, led by Sparta. Ultimately, the Spartan victory, achieved with Persian support, paved the way for a shifting political landscape that eventually saw the rise of Macedon and the decline of city-state dominance.": [
        {
          "prompt": 26,
          "uid": "bd51418c-aae9-4e05-ac5e-c18df592fdcc",
          "responses": [
            65,
            66,
            67
          ],
          "llm": "Claude Haiku 4.5",
          "vars": {
