            "text": 16
          },
          "metavars": {
            "__pt": "{prompt}",
            "LLM_0": "Claude Haiku 4.5"
          }
        }
      ],
      "Delete words in the following paragraph, while keeping grammaticality and readability. Only remove words, do not add any new words. Only return the revised paragraph, nothing else.\n\nParagraph:\nThe Greco-Persian Wars were a series of pivotal conflicts between the Achaemenid Empire and the city-states of Greece that occurred during much of the fifth century BC, forever changing the course of Western history. Initiated by the Persian expansion into territories held by Greek cities, these wars included legendary battles such as Marathon, Thermopylae, and Salamis, showcasing the valor and ingenuity of the vastly outnumbered Greek forces. The perseverance of Greek city-states against the might of a multinational empire was a testament to their determination to preserve their way of life, ultimately enabling the preservation of Greek culture and philosophy. The surprising Greek victories inspired a surge in confidence, leading to the Golden Age of Athens—a period marked by remarkable cultural and architectural advancements. These wars not only halted Persian expansion westward but also set the stage for the rise of Athens as a cultural and political powerhouse in the region.": [
