      "The Punic Wars were three conflicts between the Roman Republic and Carthage, taking place between 264 and 146 BC. Tensions over Sicily ignited the wars, remembered for Hannibal's crossing of the Alps during the Second Punic War. These wars witnessed naval engagements and land battles, punctuated by sieges of Saguntum and Zama. Roman victories led to the destruction of Carthage in the Third Punic War, ensuring Roman dominance. These wars facilitated Rome's transformation into an empire, setting the stage for centuries of Roman influence.",
