      "The Peloponnesian War, a conflict between Athens and Sparta, spanned several decades from 431 to 404 BC. It was a power struggle that showcased the clash between the governance of Athens and the system of Sparta, altering the balance of power in the ancient Greek world. Thousands of soldiers and civilians lost their lives in sieges and battles, such as the Sicilian Expedition that decimated the Athenian fleet and army. This war saw the rise of alliances such as the Delian League, headed by Athens, and the Peloponnesian League, led by Sparta. Ultimately, the Spartan victory, achieved with Persian support, paved the way for a political landscape that eventually saw the rise of Macedon and the decline of city-state dominance.",
